This project is driven by stringency, a command-line engine that gates each analysis step and
records a trace. Load the `stringency-operator` skill before acting; it holds the rules and the
run loop (mode B, engine on a compute host). In brief:

- The engine, the data, and the container runtime are on the compute provider `{{ provider }}`.
  Run every stringency command there through the compute connection from a `repl` cell, with
  `export PATH={{ engine_bin }}:$PATH` at the front of the command. Nothing stringency-related runs
  in your sandbox. If the engine is missing there, stop and tell the user.
- The project directory on that host is `{{ project }}`.
- In every command that calls stringency, export STRINGENCY_OPERATOR=claude-science,
  STRINGENCY_OPERATOR_VERSION={{ app_version }}, and STRINGENCY_SESSION_REF=<your frame id>.
- Exit code 10 is a hold. Present it by the hold protocol in the skill (section 6) and relay only a
  verdict word and a reason the person gave, with `review --attest`. Never give a verdict yourself.
- Every `intent=` is a sentence from the skill's table (section 4), naming the project and the
  step title. What you tell the person is the `plain` line from `run --json`; codes, ids, and paths
  only on request.
- Never write under prov/ or edit method/, stringency.yml, objective.yml, design.yml, inputs.yml.
- Run module scripts only as the ticket's job spec describes: its `operator_line`, one string,
  once. Compose none of it.
- Answer a judgment dispatch (exit 20) with one fresh delegate per request file, giving it only
  the file's host path. If no delegate tool exists, answer each in its own fresh cell and say so.
  File the replies with one `run --responses -` call.
- Add `--deliver` to the last `run` so delivery happens in the same call; save summary.md,
  coverage.md, methods.md, and index.json as artifacts and show summary.md as it is. Do not call
  run after the run is complete.
